# Waitlist signup endpoint — the Loops form this site posts to.
#
#   https://app.loops.so/api/newsletter-form/<form-id>
#
# The <form-id> is the last path segment of the form's URL in the Loops dashboard
# (app.loops.so/forms/<form-id>). It is public — it ships in the JS bundle and in Loops' own embed
# snippet — but it is left blank here on purpose: copying this file to .env must not give a
# developer a live submitter. With no endpoint set, `npm run dev` renders the form and posts
# nothing, and a production build shows the GitHub fallback instead.
#
# Set the real value in the Render dashboard (render.yaml marks it sync: false), and in a local
# .env only when you actually intend to write to the live audience.
#
# SECURITY: everything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the public JS bundle. This must stay a
# public, unauthenticated form endpoint. Never put a Loops API key here — it would ship to every
# visitor.
#
# BEFORE THIS GOES LIVE, in the Loops dashboard:
#   1. Settings → Sending → Double opt-in: ON.
#      The page promises a confirmation email and only emails confirmed addresses. Without this
#      the copy on the page and in /privacy/ is untrue.
#   2. Customise the opt-in email under Transactional so it says what the confirmation is for.
#   3. Note that Loops keeps unconfirmed contacts as "Pending" indefinitely. /privacy/ promises
#      they are deleted when the announcement goes out — that is a manual step at that time.
VITE_WAITLIST_ENDPOINT=

# Only needed if the provider does not call the field "email". Loops takes "email", so this is
# the default and normally needs no value. (Buttondown's API wants "email_address".)
VITE_WAITLIST_FIELD=email
